    "question": "I run 12 miles in 90 minutes. What is my average speed in miles per hour?",
    "gold": "8",
    "answer": "First convert 90 minutes to hours: 90 minutes / 60 minutes/hours = <<90/60=1.5>>1.5 hours.\nIn 1 hour, I run 12 miles / 1.5 hours = <<12/1.5=8>>8 miles/hour.\n#### 8"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average speed in miles per hour, we need to determine the total distance traveled and the total time taken, and then use the formula for average speed:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average speed} = \\frac{\\text{Total distance}}{\\text{Total time}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we know the total distance is 12 miles. Next, we need to convert the total time from minutes to hours. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we can convert 90 minutes to hours by dividing 90 by 60:\n\n\\[\n90 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{90}{60} \\text{ hours} = 1.5 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNow we can substitute the total distance and the total time into the formula for average speed:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average speed} = \\frac{12 \\text{ miles}}{1.5 \\text{ hours}} = 8 \\text{ miles per hour}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the average speed is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
